/-!
# The different is locally principal when the relative dualizing module is invertible

Let `f : Y ⟶ X` be a flat locally quasi-finite morphism of locally Noetherian schemes, let
`ω_{Y/X}` be its relative dualizing module and let `τ_{Y/X} ∈ Γ(Y, ω_{Y/X})` be its trace
element. If `ω_{Y/X}` is an invertible `𝒪_Y`-module then the closed subscheme `R ⊆ Y` defined
by the different `𝔇_f` is locally principal: every point of `Y` has an affine open
neighbourhood on which `𝔇_f` is generated by a single section.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Discriminant.isQuasicoherent_different`: the different is quasi-coherent, so it is the
  ideal sheaf of a closed subscheme.
* `Stacks.Discriminant.isLocallyPrincipal_different`: the closed subscheme defined by the
  different is a locally principal closed subscheme of `Y`.

## Implementation notes

The closed subscheme `R` is spelled as the ideal sheaf datum that cuts it out,
`Stacks.Divisors.idealSheafDataOfSubmodule (different ω τ)`: the different of
[Stacks, Tag 0BW4] is a submodule sheaf of `𝒪_Y`, while local principality of
[Stacks, Tag 01WR] is stated for `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData`, and the two readings
of a quasi-coherent ideal subsheaf correspond by Tag 01QQ. On an affine open the ideal of the
datum is the ideal of sections of the different.

The ambient category is `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules`, written `Y.Modules`. The two
spellings `Y.Modules` and `SheafOfModules Y.ringCatSheaf` of the category of `𝒪_Y`-modules have
the same underlying type but carry different `CategoryTheory.Category` instances, so a cokernel
formed at one is not found by instance search at the other.

Part (2) of [Stacks, Tag 0BWA], that the norm of `R` is the discriminant `D_f` when `f` is
finite, is `Stacks.Discriminant.discriminantIdeal_eq_normIdealSheaf_differentIdealSheaf`, an
equality of ideal sheaves on `X`. Part (3), that when `f` is étale at the associated points of
`Y` the subscheme `R` is an effective Cartier divisor and `𝒪_Y(R) ≅ ω_{Y/X}`, is
`Stacks.Discriminant.isEffectiveCartierDivisor_differentIdealSheaf` and
`Stacks.Discriminant.existsUnique_invertibleSheafIso_differentIdealSheaf`; it uses Tag 0BW9 and
Tag 01X0.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BWA](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BWA)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BW4](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BW4)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01WR](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01WR)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01QQ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01QQ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B8M](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B8M)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02OM](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02OM)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite TopologicalSpace
open RingedSpaceModuleAdjunction
open scoped AlgebraicGeometry

attribute [local implicit_reducible] SheafOfModules.unit PresheafOfModules.unit
  PresheafOfModules.presheaf TopCat.Sheaf Scheme.Modules

-- The different is a submodule of the unit of `structureSheafRing Y.toRingedSpace`, while
-- `Y.Modules` is indexed by `Y.ringCatSheaf = (sheafCompose _ (forget₂ _ _)).obj Y.sheaf`. The
-- two sheaves of rings are equal by `rfl`, and instance search has to see that: the coherence
-- of the different is proved at the first index and consumed at the second. Reaching one from
-- the other needs these two Mathlib definitions unfoldable during instance search.
attribute [local instance_reducible] CategoryTheory.sheafCompose
  AlgebraicGeometry.SheafedSpace.sheaf

universe u

namespace Stacks.Discriminant

variable {X Y : Scheme.{u}} {f : Y ⟶ X}
  [IsLocallyNoetherian X] [IsLocallyNoetherian Y] [Flat f] [LocallyQuasiFinite f]

/-- The different is a quasi-coherent `𝒪_Y`-module. -/
instance isQuasicoherent_different (ω : RelativeDualizingModuleData f)
    (τ : RelativeTraceSection ω) :
    ((different ω τ).toSheafOfModules : Y.Modules).IsQuasicoherent :=
  haveI : _root_.SheafOfModules.IsCoherent ((different ω τ).toSheafOfModules : Y.Modules) :=
    (_root_.SheafOfModules.isCoherent_iff _).mpr (isCoherent_different ω τ)
  (Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.CoherentTFAE.isQuasicoherent_isFiniteType_of_isCoherent
    ((different ω τ).toSheafOfModules : Y.Modules)).1

/-- **[Stacks, Tag 0BWA (1)].** Let `f : Y ⟶ X` be a flat locally quasi-finite morphism of
locally Noetherian schemes with relative dualizing module `ω_{Y/X}` and trace element
`τ_{Y/X}`. If `ω_{Y/X}` is an invertible `𝒪_Y`-module, then the closed subscheme `R ⊆ Y`
defined by the different `𝔇_f` is a locally principal closed subscheme. -/
@[stacks 0BWA "part (1)"]
theorem isLocallyPrincipal_different (ω : RelativeDualizingModuleData f)
    (τ : RelativeTraceSection ω)
    [Stacks.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible Y.presheaf
      (structureSheafRing
        Y.toRingedSpace).property ω.sheaf] :
    Stacks.Divisors.IsLocallyPrincipal
      (Stacks.Divisors.idealSheafDataOfSubmodule (different ω τ)) := by
  intro y
  obtain ⟨W, hyW, hW⟩ :=
    Stacks.SheafOfModules.Scheme.exists_nonempty_linearEquiv_of_isInvertible Y ω.sheaf y
  obtain ⟨_, ⟨V, hV, rfl⟩, hyV, hVW⟩ :=
    Y.isBasis_affineOpens.exists_subset_of_mem_open hyW W.isOpen
  obtain ⟨e⟩ := hW V hVW
  refine ⟨⟨V, hV⟩, hyV, ?_⟩
  set t : Γ(ω.sheaf, V) := (traceHom ω τ).app V (1 : Γ(Y, V))
  refine ⟨e t, ?_⟩
  have hmap : Submodule.map (e : Γ(ω.sheaf, V) →ₗ[Γ(Y, V)] Γ(Y, V))
      (Submodule.span Γ(Y, V) {t}) = Ideal.span {e t} := by
    rw [Submodule.map_span, Set.image_singleton]
    rfl
  have equot : (Γ(ω.sheaf, V) ⧸ Submodule.span Γ(Y, V) {t}) ≃ₗ[Γ(Y, V)]
      (Γ(Y, V) ⧸ Ideal.span {e t}) :=
    Submodule.Quotient.equiv _ _ e hmap
  have hcoker : Module.annihilator Γ(Y, V) Γ(traceCoker ω τ, V) = Ideal.span {e t} := by
    rw [← (cokernelSectionsEquiv ω τ ⟨V, hV⟩).annihilator_eq, equot.annihilator_eq]
    exact Ideal.annihilator_quotient
  exact (different_sections_eq_annihilator ω τ ⟨V, hV⟩).trans hcoker

end Stacks.Discriminant

end
